Notes
-----
This run followed a multi-round debugging cycle after the human
initially reported: "Test is passing but for AISDLC-2 testcases are
failing" (9 unexpected failures on first run). Root causes found and
fixed, each verified against a fresh Playwright HTML report parsed
directly from the local report server:

Run 1 (total=22, expected=13, unexpected=9):
  All 9 failures in library-AISDLC-2.feature.spec.js, toBeVisible
  timeouts on #members-list tbody tr. Root cause: GET /api/members
  (AISDLC-3) changed from a flat array to a paginated envelope
  ({ members, page, pageSize, total, totalPages }); the frontend
  (src/client/app.ts) still treated the response as Member[], so
  .map()/.forEach() silently failed and the members table/Issue Book
  dropdown never rendered.
  Fix: app repo PR #7 (loadMembers/loadMembersSelect read data.members).

Run 2 (total=22, unexpected=9, unchanged):
  PR #7's fetch call never actually added ?pageSize=100 despite the
  comment saying it would; default pageSize=20 vs 85 existing members
  (id ASC, oldest-first) meant new members still fell off page 1.
  Fix: app repo PR #8 (actually add ?pageSize=100 to loadMembers()).

Run 3 (total=22, unexpected=7, improved):
  Same "element not found" pattern recurring because total members
  had grown to 98 (near/over the 100 pageSize cap) — AISDLC-2 test
  scenarios create a member per run with no cleanup.
  Fix: test repo PR #3 (LoanSeeder.cleanup() deletes seeded
  loans/members/books instead of just marking loans returned).
  Also manually purged 90 stale aisdlc2.fine.* test members left
  over from prior runs (111 -> 21 members) to reset the baseline.

Run 4 (total=22, unexpected=4, improved further):
  New failure mode: "database is locked" on the loanSeeder fixture/
  After Hooks (plus 1-2 cascading timeouts/false results). Root
  cause: playwright.config.ts fullyParallel workers each open a
  separate node:sqlite connection to the same shared library.db as
  the app server, with no busy_timeout set, so concurrent writes
  raised SQLITE_BUSY immediately instead of retrying.
  Fix: test repo PR #4 (PRAGMA busy_timeout=5000 on the LoanSeeder
  connection; batched cleanup()'s deletes into one transaction).

Run 5 (this run): total=22, expected=22, unexpected=0. Clean pass.

All fixes have been merged to main in both repos:
  App repo:  PR #7, #8 (+ housekeeping PR #5, #6)
  Test repo: PR #3, #4

AISDLC-3 pagination scenarios: all passing.
AISDLC-2 regression scenarios: all passing (no functional regression
in fine calculation/pay/waive logic itself — failures were entirely
UI-rendering/test-infrastructure issues, now resolved).
